	(text "Digital isolator for the eFuse enable and fault signals"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 21.82 100.56 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.032 2.032)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "0277db3a-e068-55ae-b7cf-527a4c412ce7")
	)
	(text "Isolated CAN transceiver and common-mode choke"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 21.82 26.9 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.032 2.032)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "07e33e4f-daa9-526a-b007-af842ecb1451")
	)
	(text "Isolated CAN section, 2-jack single-bus version (design brief plans/isolated-can-section-brief.md, rev C1).\nThis board is the CANopen master in the middle of one linear bus:\n   [120 ohm] drive EL -- drive AZ -- J12 == this board == J13 -- weather bridge -- AZ node -- EL node [120 ohm]\nThree domains, kept apart on the board:\n   logic:        3V3_MCU, GND (the STM32 side of U17 and U18)\n   isolated CAN: 24V_ISO_IN, CAN_V+, 5V_ISO, GND_ISO (brief names +24V_ISO, +5V_ISO, GND_ISO)\n   chassis:      CHASSIS (PE in the brief): the two RJ45 shells only\nThe isolated 24 V is not the drive-I/O 24 V (DSY-C INCOM, limit loops): keep those supplies separate.\nIsolation barrier under U17 and U18: no copper on any layer, 4 mm creepage or more (8 mm with these packages)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 22.86 243.84 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.016 1.016)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "14b86792-7932-5e6b-b605-e4c1ca65f23d")
	)
	(text "Isolated CAN (CANopen)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 16 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 5 5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "155a4cc7-4671-5768-907c-1b5dc9a46c89")
	)
	(text "J12  CAN A - drives (no power)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 181.61 34.29 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "1a1a5741-7601-5cb0-8add-b2049bbb8963")
	)
	(text "GND_ISO"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 361.5 75.3 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.9 0.9)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "227b781f-b5c4-5060-b1d1-119849a9bbb7")
	)
	(text "5V_ISO supply for the isolated side"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 251.69 158.98 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.032 2.032)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "28480766-5b7c-5e1a-a50d-956fa770c835")
	)
	(text "U18 ISO7721 (DW, SOIC-16 wide, 8 mm creepage) crosses the same isolation barrier as U17.\nCAN_VBUS_EN (PC8): high or not driven = dish-side CAN_V+ on, low = off. The ISO7721 output defaults high when its input is\nopen or the logic side is unpowered, so CAN_V+ comes up without firmware.\nCAN_VBUS_FLT (PC9): low = eFuse fault, eFuse switched off, or output still ramping. It reads high when the isolated side\nhas no 24 V at all, so a high level alone does not prove that the dish segment is powered.\nC54: Y1 capacitor footprint from GND to GND_ISO, not fitted. Fit it only if emissions testing calls for it.\nNothing else may bridge the barrier. GND_ISO never connects to GND or to CHASSIS."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 22.86 141 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.9 0.9)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "347670b6-0f11-54b8-824d-0f02b108f918")
	)
	(text "+24 V\nGND_ISO"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 49.53 177.9 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "5ac398fc-842e-5420-abf4-dd0b0de0d811")
	)
	(text "CAN bus through-path, protection, termination and RJ45 jacks"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 179.3 26.9 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.032 2.032)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "6d5db719-b205-5a70-9a48-d261cc932314")
	)
	(text "J12 = CAN A, drive side (to DSY-C CN1). J13 = CAN B, dish side (weather bridge, AZ node, EL node).\nSilkscreen J13 \"CAN + 24 V OUT - DISH\": it carries power that must never reach a drive.\nBoth jacks use the CiA 303-1 pinout: pin 1 CAN_H, pin 2 CAN_L. CAN_H / CAN_L run straight from J12 to J13 as one\n120 ohm pair with no series parts; the transceiver taps off with a single short stub. One bus with two ends: do not add a third jack.\nJ12: pin 3 = GND_ISO through R52 (0 ohm link, JP_DRV_GND). Pins 4-8 not connected: no CAN_V+ toward the drives.\nJ13: pins 3 and 7 = GND_ISO, pin 8 = CAN_V+ (24 V from the eFuse, 0.5 A limit). Pins 4-6 not connected.\nTermination: SW2 OFF (default). The bus is terminated at the far drive (DSY-C DIP SW4) and at the EL axis node.\nBoth SW2 switches ON = 120 ohm split termination (R54 + R55 0.25 W, C59 C0G), only if this board sits at a bus end.\nD9 / D11: CAN ESD clamps (27 V stand-off, above CAN_V+), one at each jack. D12: CAN_V+ clamp at J13.\nShields: each jack shell goes to CHASSIS through a 0 ohm link (R49, R60). R51 + C58 and R59 + C64 are the RC\noption (1 Mohm, 4.7 nF 2 kV), not fitted: to use it, remove the 0 ohm link and fit the RC."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 181.61 128.27 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.9 0.9)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "89124781-7ec1-5f5b-999e-20c5c377bf2a")
	)
