		(uuid "cbd11ed3-b8bb-54b3-b84e-9526a96535a9")
	)
	(text "J11: 24 V from the external isolated Mean Well 48 V to 24 V converter. Its -V output stays floating: no bond to PE or to board GND.\nD8 SMBJ28CA (28 V stand-off, 45 V clamp) is bidirectional, so a reversed supply is blocked by U19 and not shorted by the TVS.\nU19 TPS26600 eFuse: current limit 12 / R43 = 0.5 A with auto-retry (MODE to RTN). Under-voltage lock-out 8.6 V rising / 8.0 V falling,\nover-voltage cut-off 34.4 V rising / 31.8 V falling (R40, R41, R42). C55 ramps CAN_V+ in about 42 ms: about 60 mA inrush into C56 + C57.\nEFUSE_RTN is the eFuse control reference (R42, R43, C55, MODE, pad). Do not join it to GND_ISO: that defeats the reverse-polarity protection.\nSHDN: R47 / R46 divide the 5 V isolator output to 3.3 V (pin limit 4 V); low = off. With U18 unpowered R46 holds the eFuse off.\nFLT: open drain, R48 pull-up. R50 limits the current into U18 if J11 is reversed (FLT can then follow RTN negative). IMON not used.\nC56 / C57: bulk capacitance on CAN_V+. Every part on the 24 V nets is rated for the 45 V clamp (100 V capacitors, 60 V eFuse).\nLED7 + R53: CAN_V+ on (2 mA). Test points for a fixture: TP34 drives the LED anode, TP32 pulls UVLO low to hold U19 off."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 22.86 217.17 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.9 0.9)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d07c9e34-6070-5357-a550-dccc4836d982")
	)
	(text "U17 ISO1042 (DW, SOIC-16 wide): isolated CAN FD transceiver, 5 Mbit/s, 5 kVrms, +/-70 V bus fault protection.\nLogic side on 3V3_MCU / GND: C46 100 nF + C48 1 uF at VCC1. Bus side on 5V_ISO / GND_ISO: this package has two VCC2 pins,\neach with its own 100 nF (C50 at pin 16, C52 at pin 11), plus C53 1 uF.\nTXD from PA12 (FDCAN1_TX) through R38, RXD to PA11 (FDCAN1_RX). The bus runs classic CAN at 500 kbit/s (DSY-C default,\nP10.09 = 0); CAN FD capability is headroom only.\nR39: TXD pull-up to 3V3_MCU. The bus stays recessive while PA12 floats during reset and boot.\nL2: common-mode choke in the transceiver stub. R44 / R45 (0 ohm, not fitted) bypass it if it causes trouble.\nLayout: stub from the through-path (CAN_H / CAN_L in the bus section) to U17 no longer than 30 mm.\nC50 and C52 on the top layer, each right at its VCC2 pin, connected without vias."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 22.86 78.74 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.9 0.9)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d1d1c8d0-bf98-5828-9a44-1c81e41ef45c")
	)
	(text "24 V isolated input and CAN_V+ eFuse (dish-side bus power)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 21.82 158.98 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.032 2.032)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d771d41c-186d-5864-bf28-86fa2eb614e8")
	)
	(text "GND_ISO"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 361.5 68.2 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.9 0.9)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e0ab9370-6b95-5f52-9848-716836911247")
	)
	(text "U20 LMR51606X: 65 V, 0.6 A synchronous buck, 400 kHz. Output 0.8 V x (1 + R57 / R58) = 5.07 V.\nLoad: U17 up to about 75 mA while it drives the bus dominant, U18 about 2 mA.\nD10 feeds it from the input side of the eFuse: U17 keeps talking to the drives while CAN_V+ is\nswitched off. D10 also blocks a reversed supply.\nL3 33 uH (1.65 A saturation, above the 1.4 A maximum switch limit) and C63 22 uF are the datasheet\nvalues for 5 V at 400 kHz. C60 / C61: 100 V input capacitors.\nEN: R56 pulls it up to VIN; a test fixture can hold U20 off at TP39.\nLayout: keep the switch node (U20 pin 6, L3, C62) away from the CAN pair and the isolation barrier."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 252.73 210.82 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.9 0.9)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "f9ce4921-7b73-5414-9651-7d6593966cb4")
	)
